title: $:/plugins/mblackman/tiddlypwa/notifications

\define tv-wikilinks() no

!!! Developing Push Notifications in Your Wiki

TiddlyPWA provides three tiers for authoring Web Push notifications in your wiki or plugins. Enable push on your device first under ''$:/ControlPanel'' → ''TiddlyPWA'' → ''Push Notifications''.

---

!!!! Tier 1: Sandboxed Server Watchers (`module-type: pwa-watcher`)

Run a JavaScript ES module on the server on a cron schedule to poll RSS/Atom feeds, JSON APIs, or web pages while your devices are offline.

''Required Tiddler Fields:''
* `type`: `application/javascript`
* `module-type`: `pwa-watcher`
* `watcher-id`: unique ID (e.g. `my.hn.rss`)
* `schedule-cron`: 5-field cron (e.g. `0 * * * *`)
* `allowed-hosts`: comma-separated hostnames (e.g. `news.ycombinator.com`)
* `config-filter` (optional): filter of tiddlers passed in `context.items`
* `enabled` (optional): `yes` (default) or `no`

''Module Signature & `host` API:''
```javascript
export async function evaluate(context, host) {
	// host.fetch(url, opts?) -> { ok, status, notModified, body, headers }
	// host.parseXml(xml) -> { items: [{ title, link, guid, pubDate, description }] }
	// host.queryHtml(html, selector) -> [{ tag, text, html, attrs }]
	// host.extractJsonLd(html, type?) -> object[]
	// host.matchRegex(str, pattern, flags?) -> string[][]
	// host.getState(key) / host.setState(key, value)
	const res = await host.fetch('https://news.ycombinator.com/rss');
	if (!res.ok || res.notModified) return [];
	const feed = await host.parseXml(res.body);
	const top = feed.items[0];
	if (!top || (await host.getState('lastGuid')) === top.guid) return [];
	await host.setState('lastGuid', top.guid);

	return [{
		notify: {
			title: 'Top HN Story',
			body: top.title,
			openUrl: top.link, // or navigateTo: 'HN: ' + top.title, or clickAction: 'none'
			actions: [{ action: 'open-wiki', title: 'Open in Wiki' }]
		},
		createTiddler: {
			title: 'HN: ' + top.title,
			text: top.link,
			tags: ['HN']
		},
		actionPatches: {
			'open-wiki': { navigateTo: 'HN: ' + top.title }
		}
	}];
}
```

Trigger a watcher manually with `<$action-sendmessage $message="tm-pwa-run-watcher" watcher-id="my.hn.rss"/>`.

---

!!!! Tier 2: Declarative Due-Date Rules (`$:/tags/NotificationRule`)

Schedule client-encrypted notifications automatically from tiddler date fields.

''Rule Tiddler Fields:''
* `tags`: `$:/tags/NotificationRule`
* `filter`: e.g. `[tag[Task]!tag[Done]has[due]]`
* `date-field`: field holding due date/time (default: `due`; supports TW 14/17-digit timestamps, `YYYY-MM-DD`, `YYYYMMDD`, or ISO strings)
* `default-time`: local `HH:mm` for date-only values (default: `09:00`)
* `offset-minutes`: minutes offset (e.g. `-15` for 15 minutes before due)
* `title-template`: e.g. `Task Due: {{!!title}}`
* `body-template`: e.g. `Due: {{!!due}}`
* `navigate-to` / `url-field` / `open-url` / `click-action`: configure click target (`navigate`, `url`, or `none`)

---

!!!! Tier 3: Ad-Hoc Widget Messages (`tm-pwa-schedule-notification`)

Schedule or cancel client-encrypted one-off notifications from buttons or scripts:

```tid
<$button>
  <$action-sendmessage
    $message="tm-pwa-schedule-notification"
    id="my-timer"
    delay-seconds="300"
    title="Timer Complete"
    body="5 minutes elapsed!"
    navigate-to="My Timer"
    scope="device"
  />
  Start 5m Timer
</$button>

<$button>
  <$action-sendmessage $message="tm-pwa-cancel-notification" id="my-timer"/>
  Cancel Timer
</$button>
```
